        "description": "A ninth consecutive night of strikes, the US said it targeted Iranian missile and drone launch sites, as well as communication networks. US President Donald Trump said the attacks are in honour of three US troops killed in recent days.\n \nIt\u2019s emerged that two of those three US service members were killed in Iranian strikes on a US base in Jordan, the third was killed after an Iranian attack in northern Iraq.\n \nIran has retaliated firing at US interests in the Gulf, both Kuwait and Bahrain have reported incoming fire.\n \nMeanwhile, oil rises to its highest price in a month after Iran said it had also attacked two oil tankers trying to transit through the Strait of Hormuz. \n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#IranWar #BBCNews #BBCNews",
