        "date_published": "2026-07-20T06:30:25+00:00",
        "description": "Andy Burnham will become the UK's prime minister today, replacing Keir Starmer .\n\nStarmer will deliver his final address as PM later this morning, before he and Burnham visit King Charles in Buckingham Palace.\n \nThe new prime minister will then give his own speech in Downing Street - he will promise \"more breathing room\" for Britain, while arguing for a more \"stable and responsible\" politics.\n\nTory leader Kemi Badenoch wished the new PM \"every success\" - but warns he is entering Downing Street without a \"clear plan\u201d.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#UKPolitics #BBCNews",
